# More width and cluster cases: CJK punctuation, fullwidth forms, zero
# width characters, wide characters and editing, and REP.
@cite https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr29/

@case Fullwidth Latin is wide
@size 10x2
@send "\u{FF21}x"
@expect-screen
|Ａ‹x·······|

@case Halfwidth katakana is narrow
@size 10x2
@send "\u{FF76}x"
@expect-screen
|ｶx········|

@case CJK punctuation is wide
@size 10x2
@send "\u{3002}x"
@expect-screen
|。‹x·······|

@case Hangul syllables are wide
@size 10x2
@send "한x"
@expect-screen
|한‹x·······|

@case ZWSP takes no cell
@size 10x2
@send "a\u{200B}b"
@expect-cursor 1,3

@case A soft hyphen takes a cell
@size 10x2
@send "a\u{AD}b"
@expect-cursor 1,4

@case Two combining marks stack on one cell
@size 10x2
@send "a\u{301}\u{323}b"
@expect-cursor 1,3

@case A combining mark after CUP joins the cell to the left
@size 10x2
@send "ab\e[1;2H\u{301}"
@expect-cursor 1,2

@case Wide characters wrap as a unit
@size 5x2
@send "日本語"
@expect-screen
|日‹本‹·|
|語‹···|

@case A wide character after DECAWM off at the edge is dropped at the last column
@size 5x2
@send "\e[?7l\e[1;5H日"
@expect-cursor 1,5

@case ICH splitting a wide character clears it
@size 10x2
@send "a日b\e[1;3H\e[@"
@expect-screen
|a···b·····|

@case ECH on the right half clears the whole character
@size 10x2
@send "日b\e[1;2H\e[X"
@expect-screen
|··b·······|

@case REP repeats a wide character
@size 10x2
@send "日\e[2b"
@expect-screen
|日‹日‹日‹····|

@case REP repeats a combining cluster
@size 10x2
@send "e\u{301}\e[1b"
@expect-screen
|éé········|

@case Emoji modifier with mode 2027 is one cluster
@size 10x2
@mode-2027 on
@send "\u{1F44D}\u{1F3FD}x"
@expect-screen
|👍🏽‹x·······|

@case Keycap sequence with mode 2027 is wide
@size 10x2
@mode-2027 on
@send "1\u{FE0F}\u{20E3}x"
@expect-screen
|1️⃣‹x·······|

@case VS15 with mode 2027 keeps text presentation
@size 10x2
@mode-2027 on
@send "\u{2764}\u{FE0E}x"
@expect-cursor 1,3

@case Invalid UTF-8 prints U+FFFD
@size 10x2
@send "a\xffb"
@expect-screen
|a�b·······|

@case A truncated sequence before ESC prints U+FFFD
@size 10x2
@send "a\xe6\e[1mb"
@expect-screen
|a�b·······|

@case Mode 2027 reports set
@size 10x2
@mode-2027 on
@send "\e[?2027$p"
@expect-reply "\e[?2027;1$y"
